=== PARITY (vs web StatChartSlide.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> the web slide takes a resolved `data: YearReview` prop (`useTranslation` is its only
    hook; the parent story owns the query). The native surface binds that prop through the P1/S8
    StatChartSlideSource seam (`init(data:)` maps `<StatChartSlide data />` onto the content branch) and
    additionally carries the full cache-then-network load state so the P4 contract's loading/empty/
    error/stale/offline chrome can render. The view performs NO HTTP. useTranslation -> the P1/S10
    StatChartSlideStrings facade.
  Projection -> StatChartSlideProjection.make is a 1:1 port of the web body: the `chartData` memo
    (`monthly_stats.map(m => ({ name: MONTH_LABELS[m.month-1] ?? `M${m.month}`, drives: m.drives }))`),
    the `AnimatedNumber` total (`fmtNumber(total_drives, 0)` -> "1,284"), and the average caption
    (`t('yearReview.avgPerWeek', { count: fmtNumber(avg_drives_per_week, 1) })` -> "24.7 drives per week
    on average"). fmtNumber is ported with halfExpand rounding + non-finite->0. Out-of-range month ->
    "M13" exactly like the web `?? `M${month}``. Verified by executed XCTest.
  Composition -> the web centered column (`flex flex-col items-center justify-center h-full px-6
    text-center`): the 🗓️ emoji (web spring stiffness:200 damping:15 -> SwiftUI spring pop-in), the
    counting drive total beside the localized "drives" label, the average-per-week caption, and the
    drives-by-month bar chart. The web `motion` entrance delays (number 0.2s, caption 0.5s, chart 0.7s)
    map to TSFadeIn delays; the from-zero count-up reproduces the web `AnimatedNumber`'s RAF ease-out
    ramp via an Animatable view. Bars use the brand `chartSeriesPower` token (web violet
    `rgba(167,139,250,0.7)`), rounded tops (web `radius=[4,4,0,0]`), faint grid + unlabelled axes (web
    CartesianGrid + axisLine/tickLine=false).
  Shared components -> @/components/data-display (AnimatedNumber) -> the from-zero StatChartSlideAnimatedTotal
    (the shared TSAnimatedNumber is a fixed-size numericText transition, not a from-zero count-up; the
    web component's actual behaviour is reproduced at hero size via Font.TS.display). @/components/motion
    (FadeIn) -> TSFadeIn. @/components/charts (Recharts BarChart) -> a dedicated Swift Charts view (the
    generic TSBarChart lacks per-bar VoiceOver + the slide's single-series styling, so a bespoke chart
    is built exactly as the MonthlyMileageWidget dashboard chart does). Compiled against the REAL
    apps/apple design+component closure (generated Tokens + Sources/Design + Sources/Components, minus
    the SI UnitFormatters file the slide does not use) in the iOS+macOS typechecks below. Recharts ->
    Swift Charts / Leaflet -> none.
  States (all render) -> loading(skeleton chrome) · content(hero + chart) · empty(friendly "no drives
    recorded yet") · error(+retry) · stale(content + stale chip + auto-refresh) · offline(cached content
    + offline chip, or offline-no-data + retry). The web leaf only ever renders content; the loading/
